From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm exl3: TF_GLM_OVN_EY_DIRECT, a prompt chunk's routed down kernel writes the slot rows itself

Ported from our archived fork `ai-engine` (ref `fork-ssh/ovn-up`): the EY_DIRECT part of f9209395e "glm cuda: TF_GLM_OVN
prompt expert switches for EXL3 prompts" (the fork's docs/research/overnight-2026-10-29/impl-x3prompt.md section 1;
production does the same, exl3_mm.py routed(..., y = b.ey.view(-1, D))). Hand ported: the fork's kernel is odown<0> of a
new exl3_prompt_ovn.cuh behind a switch struct read when the kernels load; here tf_exl3_ovn_down_0 sits beside
tf_exl3_prompt_down in exl3_experts.cu with that kernel's body and one more line (the store row), the knob is read where
the buffers are sized and travels on the family's Scratch, and the common prompt run takes an optional `Out`.

Left out, and why:
- X3_PROMPT_K64 (production's ots0106/ots0127 64-k stages), X3_PROMPT_ORDER and its order kernel: other levers of the
  same commit, each its own patch with its own receipts.
- X3_YBF16 (bf16 slot rows): a numerics trade.
- The fork's Ovn struct in cuda/exl3_prompt.zig and its read at kernel load: one knob does not need it, and reading it
  in Buffers.make gives the arena's size and the launch one source, so they cannot disagree.

What the knob does (default off; a .glm row of platform/environment.zig read through cuda/ovn.zig): with
TF_GLM_OVN_EY_DIRECT=1, Buffers.make sizes a prompt buffer's EXL3 arena without the 8-slot y
(exl3.scratchBytes(..., true): common.prompt.directBytes, 268,435,456 bytes less a rank at 2,048 rows) and sets
Scratch.ey_direct. cuda_exl3.run then gives each call's ey rows to the common prompt run as an `Out` (ey + at * 9 *
dims * 4, 9 slot rows a row), which launches tf_exl3_ovn_down_0 in place of tf_exl3_prompt_down, and the copy of the
call's routed slots (cuMemcpy2D, y to ey) is not issued. Decode windows are untouched (their item plan already writes
ey). Off: the same launches with the same arguments and the same arena; the module load looks up one more function,
which it never launches.

Bits: tf_exl3_ovn_down_0 is tf_exl3_prompt_down's main loop, sums, rotation and scale; pair p (row * 8 + slot) is
stored at row (p / 8) * 9 + p % 8 instead of p, where the copy put it (dst pitch 9 slot rows, src pitch 8). Slot 8 is
put_slot's after either. The copy was the next operation on the stream after the down launch, so nothing reads ey's
routed slots between the two in either form, and nothing but that copy reads y (its readers: tf_exl3_prompt_down's
argument and the copy's source, both skipped with the knob; moe.x3 is read by cuda_exl3.run alone).
tf_exl3_prompt_down is not changed.

Why (lane PrefillGap's capture pf1, rank 0, cold prompts of 8,195 and 32,771 tokens, --parallel 4 --context 1048576):
798 device copies of 268,435,456 bytes on the main stream, 42 in each full 2,048-row pass (one a MoE layer: the 8-slot
y of 2,048 rows into ey), 2.200 ms each at 122.0 GB/s, 92 ms of a pass of about 1,150 ms. Expected with the knob: about
-90 ms a full pass (-8%), -0.37 s at 8k and -1.47 s at 32k, to be measured A B B A.

Receipts (lane EyDirect, 2026-11-15; base = v1.2.7 + 0001..0035, tree 685c6abb; head = base + this patch,
tree 2a07e8cf):
- scripts/gates.sh (WSL, ~/gates/ey-base-*, ey-head-*): check-native-cuda-host rc 0 (7/7 steps both), test-cuda-host
  rc 0 (383/383 steps; head 6289 of 6319 tests, base 6283 of 6313, 30 skipped each), compile-cuda-tests rc 0 (10/10),
  test-glm-ring-host, test-glm-logprobs-host, test-glm-onepass-order-host, test-rows-host rc 0, zig fmt --check rc 0;
  scripts/gate-names.sh ey-base ey-head rc 0 (no failing name on either side). test-exl3-prompt-host (not a gates.sh
  step) fails the same two names on base and head, inherited: "1024-row calls keep row and pick offsets..." and
  "decode retains the existing split-K launches" (written before 0012's item plan and 0029's 2,048-row calls).
- scripts/lean.sh base against head: base 6257 files 386 problems, head 6259 files 386 problems, 0 new; the largest
  touched file is 558 lines. `git apply --check` on the base rc 0, and base + patch equal to head file by file.
- test-glm-ey-direct-host (6 tests: the knob, the arena sizes, Buffers.make's prefill, twin and window buffers, every
  launch and copy of a prompt chunk at 1 to 2,054 rows against the knob-off plan, decode windows unchanged, the run's
  guards) and 17 host mutants, each anchored once and each killed by a named test.
- GPU, RTX 5070 Laptop (sm_120, CUDA 13.3.1 nvcc, driver 616.92), tf-cuda-test with the images the checks load:
  glm-ey-direct-check rc 0 (24 cases: widths 640 and 768, both rotation kinds, 1 / 8 / 17 / 255 / 2,048 / 2,054 rows;
  ey and the MoE layer output after put_slot and combine equal the copy path's byte for byte, the freed arena bytes left
  as filled, each case's control, the direct values one slot over, different); glm-exl3 and glm-exl3-items rc 0. Seven
  planted controls fail it by exit code: the row stride, the slot index, the second half of an item's members, the scale
  reassociated, ey one slot over, the second call's offset at 8 slots, the copy path run as well (the freed bytes).
  The slot rows are fp32 in both paths (cuda_moe.fill's bf16_slots is false for an EXL3 layer); the cache format does
